= Power stage

The output is set by the divider #component("R7"), #component("R8") into
#pin("U3", "12"), the FB pin, and appears on #net("+3V3").

#calculation(id: "CALC-2.1", title: [Output voltage], status: "current")[
  $ V_"out" = V_"ref" (1 + R_1 / R_2) = 0.8 "V" times (1 + 100 / 31.6) = 3.332 "V" $
]

#note(id: "NOTE-012", title: [Switch-node copper], target: net("SW"))[
  Keep the copper of the switch node small.
]

#measurement(id: "MEAS-010", target: net("VIN"), value: 310, unit: "mV", limit: (max: 250))

#issue(
  id: "ISS-004",
  title: [Worst-case output above +2 %],
  status: "open",
  owner: "j.berg",
  target: (component("R7"), component("R8")),
)[The top of the tolerance band exceeds the limit by 51 mV.]

#decision(
  id: "DEC-002",
  title: [Inductor for the power stage],
  status: "accepted",
  target: (component("L1"), pin("U3.3")),
)[Candidate A, 4.7 µH, 6.2 A saturation, 24 mΩ.]

#annotation(kind: "note", date: "2026-11-17")[The earlier block form still prints.]
